  "term": "abducens nerve",
  "definition": "The abducens nerve is the sixth cranial nerve. It begins in the pons and carries motor signals to the eye’s lateral rectus muscle, helping control side-to-side eye movement; injury to the nerve or its nucleus can impair horizontal eye movements.",
